# Canonical Prettier ignore list — BUILD OUTPUT ONLY.
#
# This file is the source of truth, not a drop-in: Prettier resolves a pattern
# relative to the IGNORE FILE'S OWN DIRECTORY, so a file under packages/config/
# cannot be referenced from a repo root with `--ignore-path`. Copy this list
# into the repo-root `.prettierignore` instead, above any repo-specific,
# byte-pinned exceptions.
#
# Why it exists even though Prettier 3 ignores `.gitignore`d files by default:
#  1. `--ignore-path <file>` REPLACES the default set (`.gitignore` +
#     `.prettierignore`), so a repo that passes one explicitly loses the other.
#     That was codai's `format` script until 2026-11-24.
#  2. A repo whose `.gitignore` does not list build output silently formats
#     generated files and fails its own check on them.
#
# Measured 2026-11-24: codai `prettier --check .` = 34.5 s wall / 796 MB peak.
# brivio has 382 build-output files on disk but 0 visible to Prettier, so there
# this list is defence-in-depth rather than a fix.
#
# What is NOT here on purpose: `.prettierrc`-pinned content exceptions. Those
# are repo-specific (a tracked file a formatter must not touch) and belong in
# the repo's own `.prettierignore`, below this block.

# JS/TS build output
coverage/
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Caches
.vite/
.cache/

# Rust
target/
